SUMMARY:Reeds\, Rhythm & All That Brass
DESCRIPTION:\n\n An Afternoon of Big Band Music\n\nDon't miss this glorious 
 tribute to the big band era of the 1930s and 1940s with Reeds\, Rhythm & 
 All That Brass (RRB). Featuring the music America danced and swung to 
 during World War II\, one of the most influential periods in music history. 
 RRB's performance offers a nostalgic journey\, recalling the times when 
 Americans danced in music halls across the country to the greatest 
 bandleaders in history.\n\nAbout the presenters\n\nReeds\, Rhythm\, and All 
 That Brass is a 17-piece big band that plays swing-pop standards by the 
 greats\, including Basie\, Ellington\, Goodman\, Sinatra\, and 
 Darin.\n\nFrank Sole\, Henry Nerenberg\, Jay Wilensky\, Darrell Courtley\, 
 and Jeff Rantzer are the regulars in the band.\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10341-17215055
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17215055
