SUMMARY:Auteurs and Authors with Montclair Film NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. You can register 
 here.\n\nThe Auteurs and Authors film discussion class features three new 
 films at Montclair Film Cinemas\, followed by evening library discussions. 
 (View films at your convenience.)\n\nExplore how great filmmakers become 
 auteurs through adaptations and literary influences.\n\nKLARA AND THE SUN 
 (Taika Waititi) — November 2. Based on Kazuo Ishiguro's novel set in a 
 near-future world\, exploring AI and what it means to be 
 human.\n\nFATHERLAND (Paweł Pawlikowski) — November 16. Author Thomas 
 Mann returns to Germany after WWII.\n\nDUNE 3 (Denis Villeneuve) — 
 December 21. The latest adaptation of Frank Herbert's epic science fiction 
 series.\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Books, Film & Theater, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-17259097
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17259097
END:VEVENT
