SUMMARY:Planning Your Financial Future: Foundations of Investing
DESCRIPTION:Building your investor IQ starts with understanding the basics. 
 Whether you are new to investing or want a refresher\, the Foundations of 
 investing discussion will help you learn about:\n\n The importance of 
 developing a workable strategy\n\n The impact of asset allocation\n\n Ideas 
 for focusing on what you can control with your finances to achieve 
 financial goals\n\nSign up for other events in this series: Retirement By 
 Design\n\nPresenter Bio:\nJose (Dre') Martin\, Chartered Retirement 
 Planning Counselor™\nJose' runs a comprehensive wealth management 
 practice at Edward Jones in Florham Park\, where he has been helping 
 families and individuals make sense of their finances.  With over 20 years 
 of experience working at Wall Street firms like JP Morgan\, Morgan 
 Stanley\, and UBS\, Jose has seen firsthand the importance of financial 
 guidance\; and he has made it his mission to share that knowledge in a way 
 that's clear\, practical\, and uplifting.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Finances
UID:LibCal-10306-17530996
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17530996
END:VEVENT
