DTEND:20261104T004500Z
DTSTAMP:20261103T000000Z
SUMMARY:'On This Ground' St. Benedict's Prep Discussion Panel with Anthony DePalma
DESCRIPTION:This is an Adult School class. Click HERE to register.\n\n"On 
 This Ground" tells the remarkable story of a school that refused to die in 
 a city that almost did. The school is St. Benedict's Prep\, the city is 
 Newark\, and the extraordinary people who accomplished this are the 
 Benedictine monks of Newark Abbey and the students they've taught for over 
 150 years. Joining author and longtime Montclair resident Anthony DePalma 
 will be Anthony Badger\, a member of the first class in the reimagined St. 
 Benedict's in 1973\, and Jared Boone\, St. Benedict's class of 2013\, who 
 is now program partner for the Schumann Fund for New Jersey. Both men gave 
 back to St. Benedict's by teaching there before moving on to 
 community-based careers. Both lived in Newark during their time as students 
 at St. Benedict's and witnessed the many ways in which the resilience of 
 the monks and their school helped stabilize the city during its darkest 
 days\, including the 1967 civil disturbances and the recent pandemic 
 shutdown. We'll go over important ways that other schools can learn from 
 and adapt some of St. Benedict's winning ways.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-17280979
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17280979
END:VEVENT
