DTSTART:20261105T230000Z
DTEND:20261106T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261105T000000Z
SUMMARY:Rory Gilmore's Book Club (Fable Integrated)
DESCRIPTION:This book club is integrated with the reading app Fable. You 
 will receive an email invite when you register\; join virtually to discuss 
 each chapter and vote on our next read! (Please allow up to 1 business day 
 to receive the invite link\, this email is not automated)\n\n\nVirtual 
 Buddy Read begins: Oct. 5\nIn-Person Meeting: Nov. 5\n\n"I live in two 
 worlds. One is a world of books. I’ve been a resident of Faulkner’s 
 Yoknapatawpha County\, hunted the white whale aboard the Pequod\, fought 
 alongside Napoleon\, sailed a raft with Huck and Jim\, committed 
 absurdities with Ignatius J. Reilly\, rode a sad train with Anna Karenina 
 and strolled down Swann’s Way..."\n\nRory Gilmore's Book Club is not only 
 for fans of Gilmore Girls\, it's for anyone who wants to explore the 
 classics and challenge themselves by reading directly from the Rory Gilmore 
 Reading List. We'll meet every other month at the library with coffee and 
 treats to discuss our chosen book (please feel free to bring your favorite 
 coffee mug!). We'll also be chatting virtually along the way thanks to the 
 reading app Fable! Once you register for our book club\, an invite link 
 will be sent and you can join the app\, granting you the ability to comment 
 forum-style on each chapter as well as vote for our next book. Our virtual 
 buddy read will begin on October 5\, but please feel free to join in at any 
 time!\n\nIf virtual book clubs aren't your thing\, you're also welcome to 
 simply meet up in-person to discuss the book as a whole.\n\nAll are 
 welcome! ♡\n\nNovember: The Virgin Suicides by Jeffrey Eugenides 
 (available via BCCLS\, audiobook via Hoopla)\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion, Book Club
UID:LibCal-10306-17435628
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17435628
END:VEVENT
