SUMMARY:Crochet for Beginners: Pt 1
DESCRIPTION:A two-session workshop for adults with Jessica Pollack\, JFP 
 Handmade Crafts\n\n**Registration for this program is required and opens on 
 October 25. Registration and waitlists will remain open until the date of 
 the initial session.\n**Participants register for the class with the 
 understanding that they are committing to both sessions\, to be held on 
 consecutive Sunday afternoons.\n\nLearn from fiber artist Jessica Pollack 
 in this two-week workshop designed to introduce participants to the 
 fundamentals of crochet in a relaxed\, beginner-friendly 
 setting.\n\nSession 1: Nov 8\, 2pm-4pm\nParticipants will learn basic 
 crochet skills and techniques\, including how to hold a hook and yarn\, 
 create a slip knot and chain\, and work basic stitches while practicing 
 tension and consistency.\n\nSession 2: Nov 15\, 2pm-4pm\nParticipants will 
 apply their new skills to create a simple\, functional project: a crocheted 
 bookmark. By the end of the workshop\, participants will have gained 
 foundational crochet skills and completed a project they can use and 
 enjoy.\n\nAll materials will be provided. This workshop is designed for 
 adults with no prior experience.
LOCATION:Literacy Room\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10341-17302587
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17302587
END:VEVENT
