X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ics Kstx8Swyw669Kakgqa 6478083 Ics": "https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2186006684"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ics_kstx8swyw669kakgqa_6478083_ics
SUMMARY:Midday Meetup - Estate Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T141500
DTSTAMP:20261029T000314Z
UID:TU2186006684
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T123000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261012T213850Z
DESCRIPTION:**Midday MeetUp**   \nA monthly gathering to make connections
  and learn together.  \n12:30pm Catered Lunch (free)  \n1:15pm  Featured 
 Program   \n  \n**Topic** - Estate Planning: Four documents. Two tax sys
 tems. One integrated plan.  \n**Presenter** - Linda F. Spiegel\, Esq   \
 n  \n**Cost:** FREE or Suggested Donation of $10 per person to offset cos
 ts. (Bill My Account is only open to Shomrei Members)  \n  \n**RSVP:** Re
 quired so we know how much food to buy.  \nhttps://shomrei.easyshul.com/ev
 ents/6ad0ffd03e7684002567f097  \n  \n**\\***Members should use their fob t
 o access the building.  \n  \n**About the Program**  \nJoin Linda F. Spieg
 el for an overview of four essential estate planning documents: three that
  protect your wishes during your lifetime and one that guides the distribu
 tion of your estate after death. Learn how New Jersey’s inheritance tax 
 and the federal estate tax fit into one integrated plan for your future.  
 \n  \n**About the Speaker**  \nLinda F. Spiegel\, Esq.is an Elder Care Pla
 nning mediator and works with families to help them with issues arising fr
 om aging relatives. When she is not mediating or arbitrating Ms. Spiegel w
 orks with individuals\, couples and families in estate planning. She is al
 so a divorce mediator assisting couples to reach an amicable resolution of
  their issues.  \n  \nMs. Spiegel graduated from Barnard College\, Columbi
 a University and the Boston University School of Law. She is the Chair of 
 the American Bar Association’s Senior Lawyers Division Alternate Dispute
  Resolution (ADR) Committee. In January. she was inducted into the Nationa
 l Academy of Distinguished Neutrals and is a recipient of a Joint Resoluti
 on of the Senate and General Assembly of the State of New Jersey for her w
 ork as a volunteer attorney with Project SARAH\, Stop Abusive Relationship
 s at Home.  \n  \nAdditional_Dates_for_for_Midday_MeetUps: https://shomrei
 .org/calendar/midday-meetup-calendar  \n  \n**Questions?** Contact Office
    \noffice@shomrei.org   \n  \n\\#middaymeetup\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T214437Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL;VALUE=URI:https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2186006684
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
END:VEVENT
