SUMMARY:Winter Sowing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The Glen Ridge Public Library native seed free library will 
 open in mid-November with free seeds.  Planting native plants\, leaving the 
 leaves\, and not using pesticides is a huge help to native insects and the 
 birds that rely upon them to rear their young.  Winter sowing of the free 
 seeds available through the library is an easy\, low cost way to add native 
 plants to your landscaping.  In this free workshop we will explain how to 
 prepare your native seeds to they are ready to grow next spring.  This 
 process is called cold stratification\, which will be explained with a 
 how-to demonstration of various methods you can use.  Thanksgiving to early 
 January is the perfect time to winter sow seeds and start the cold 
 stratification process.  We will also answer questions about the seeds in 
 the library and make recommendations on which plants you might wish to 
 grow.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10286-17822730
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17822730
END:VEVENT
