SUMMARY:Introduction to Spinning Wool
DESCRIPTION:An America 250 Program\n\nTake a step back in time and learn 
 how to spin wool with fiber artist Reilly Grant of Clover Folk Studio. 
 \n\nThis hands-on class will teach you about fiber arts from sheep to 
 shawl\, including the role that spinning has played in various chapters of 
 United States history. Join us to learn how to prepare wool for spinning\, 
 watch a demonstration on a spinning wheel\, and get the chance to try for 
 yourself.\n\nThis workshop is for adults. No experience necessary\, and all 
 supplies and tools will be provided. While participants will engage in 
 hands-on practice\, they will not be creating a project to take home. 
 \n\nRegistration is required.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Craft
UID:LibCal-10341-17302649
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17302649
END:VEVENT
