SUMMARY:Astrology 101: What's Your Sign?
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, December 10\, 2026 from 6:00 PM to 8:00 PM.\n\nNo 
 registration required! \n\nLet's talk astrology! This program will provide 
 a basic overview of Western astrology\, including the twelve zodiac signs\, 
 the four elements and three modalities\, the ten traditional planets\, and 
 the five major aspects.\n\nThis program is a lecture-style PowerPoint 
 presentation with Q&A woven throughout. The focus here is not on "sun sign 
 astrology" (analyzing personalities based simply on the twelve zodiac 
 signs)\, but rather on gaining a bird's eye view of the larger astrological 
 system\, of which sun signs are just one part. You will leave the program 
 with the information you need to look at an astrology chart and decode its 
 many glyphs — the ancient symbols that represent the key foundational 
 concepts of this archetypal language.\n\nAttendees are strongly encouraged 
 to look up their natal charts in advance on any number of free websites 
 (for example\, astro.com). Although Kate will not have time to provide 
 personalized chart interpretations\, you will be invited to apply key 
 concepts to your own chart as we go. (Hard copy or digital is fine.)  You 
 may also want to bring a notebook and pen.\n\nWhile Astrology 101 is 
 designed with total beginners in mind\, some familiarity with the twelve 
 zodiac signs\, especially your own sign\, is helpful. More intermediate 
 astrology learners may benefit from this jam-packed review of foundational 
 concepts.\n\nAbout the presenter: Kate Sheridan\, a.k.a. The Laundress\, is 
 a tarot reader and astrologer who believes that each one of us can make our 
 own magic. Her approach is healing rather than predictive\, and her work is 
 deeply informed by Jungian psychology. You can find her on Instagram 
 @themodernlaundress or online at thelaundresstarot.com.\n\n
LOCATION:Nutley - Stockton Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10315-17779987
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17779987
END:VEVENT
