SUMMARY:Optimizing React Apps
DESCRIPTION:NJ Code & Coffee\nIs your React app slow\, and you're not sure
  why? Join us for a hands-on talk on React performance — no theory-only 
 slides\, every claim gets proven live.\n\nCharles Inwald walks through the
  real culprits behind sluggish React apps — unnecessary re-renders\, mis
 placed state and Context\, unvirtualized lists\, bloated bundles — and f
 ixes each one live\, on stage\, with side-by-side "Slow vs. Fast" demos ti
 med in the browser.\n\n**Doors open at 2pm\, talk starts at 3pm\, arrive e
 arly for networking and light refreshments.**\n\nJoin the NJ Code & Coffee
  Community Discord - come hang out before and after:\n[www.codeandcoffee.c
 hat](http://www.codeandcoffee.chat/)\n\n**The Speaker:** Charles Inwald- F
 ull Stack Developer\, React enthusiast\, previously worked at Apple and st
 artups
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/nj-code-coffee/events/317213249/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261031T000208Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261031T000208Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
